{"data": [{"author_id": "497231011", "created_at": "2026-10-24T20:53:37.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114098005934780817"], "id": "2114098005934780817", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 322, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "\"North Korea leader Kim Jong-un visited neighboring #China on Saturday in his 1st visit there in more than a year, meeting w/a senior official &amp; declaring gratitude for Beijing’s decades of support, according to 🇨🇳 state media\"\nhttps://t.co/01wTRtv5Jp", "url": "https://x.com/ChinaBeigeBook/status/2114098005934780817"}, {"author_id": "497231011", "created_at": "2026-10-24T20:49:33.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114096984223093218"], "id": "2114096984223093218", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 390, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "\"#China's ruling Communist Party announced key personnel changes in 6 provinces on Saturday, including 2 new provincial party chiefs &amp; ​6 officials positioned to become governors, before it holds a closed-door conclave in Beijing ‌from Oct 26-29\"\nhttps://t.co/NC3Z2xaI30", "url": "https://x.com/ChinaBeigeBook/status/2114096984223093218"}, {"author_id": "14096763", "created_at": "2026-10-24T20:32:19.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114092644913623197"], "id": "2114092644913623197", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 9, "impression_count": 8123, "like_count": 90, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 16, "retweet_count": 2}, "text": "I’m on day 4 of the @willystaley / @JDVance diet of nothing but meat and fermented vegetables and I have to say I’ve been feeling great. My brain got rewired so fast. Basically the only thing I crave anymore is kimchi.", "url": "https://x.com/TheStalwart/status/2114092644913623197"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2114058617359843328"]}, "author_id": "423769635", "created_at": "2026-10-24T18:17:13.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114058648905302115"], "id": "2114058648905302115", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 5, "impression_count": 4662, "like_count": 19, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 5, "retweet_count": 3}, "text": "US government interest expenses are among the highest in the developed world relative to GDP.\n\nSource: @bcaresearch https://t.co/b2ZNdpPceF", "url": "https://x.com/SoberLook/status/2114058648905302115"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2114051631159324672", "3_2114051631121580032"]}, "author_id": "14096763", "created_at": "2026-10-24T17:49:22.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114051637245587714"], "id": "2114051637245587714", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 734, "impression_count": 183875, "like_count": 1173, "quote_count": 23, "reply_count": 88, "retweet_count": 60}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2113668825766043779", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "We obviously haven’t had the major jobs wipeout yet. But you read stuff like this. And you read what economics students themselves are saying about working with AI (ht @odavis_h) and it’s hard not to feel like the seismic shift is on its way. https://t.co/E9vs2jkeHz https://t.co/tD1v45X4Qp", "url": "https://x.com/TheStalwart/status/2114051637245587714"}, {"author_id": "497231011", "created_at": "2026-10-24T17:17:50.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114043703987716533"], "id": "2114043703987716533", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1115, "like_count": 2, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 1}, "text": "China urges government agencies to mitigate AI job displacement\nhttps://t.co/5K2G3nfGYf", "url": "https://x.com/ChinaBeigeBook/status/2114043703987716533"}, {"author_id": "1327359720", "created_at": "2026-10-24T16:22:46.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114029845823004932"], "id": "2114029845823004932", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 27, "impression_count": 11373, "like_count": 124, "quote_count": 2, "reply_count": 18, "retweet_count": 23}, "text": "Credit spreads on all things AI are widening out enough to slow some AI projects: Apollo’s Torsten Slok. “Rates are maybe not important for AI but yields are important for AI:” Slok. “Credit markets are beginning to vote with their feet.” https://t.co/qbmBTSVxN1", "url": "https://x.com/lisaabramowicz1/status/2114029845823004932"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2114023283075031040"]}, "author_id": "423769635", "created_at": "2026-10-24T15:57:05.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114023381410705508"], "id": "2114023381410705508", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 7, "impression_count": 4766, "like_count": 14, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 3, "retweet_count": 3}, "text": "Anthropic is estimated to generate more quarterly revenue than established corporate giants including Intel, Uber, Coca-Cola, and Netflix.\n\nSource: @BoringBiz_ https://t.co/OqLIn8Cth7", "url": "https://x.com/SoberLook/status/2114023381410705508"}, {"author_id": "733647469305864195", "created_at": "2026-10-24T15:39:01.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114018834206376063"], "id": "2114018834206376063", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 18, "impression_count": 7131, "like_count": 30, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 6, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2113710774837301561", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "same dynamic played out with Agencies in the US before the global financial crisis.  Treasury issuance lagged the growth in dollar fx reserves in a big way, forcing a range of investors to in effect treat Agencies as a safe assets ....  \n\n1/2 https://t.co/Jx3QpGjoRL", "url": "https://x.com/Brad_Setser/status/2114018834206376063"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2114004270244605952"]}, "author_id": "423769635", "created_at": "2026-10-24T14:41:12.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114004283368804420"], "id": "2114004283368804420", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 6, "impression_count": 5235, "like_count": 14, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 3}, "text": "France has the OECD’s second-highest ratio of public pension spending to GDP, behind only Italy.\n\nSource: @Reuters https://t.co/EjhhbOHR5R", "url": "https://x.com/SoberLook/status/2114004283368804420"}, {"author_id": "1327359720", "created_at": "2026-10-24T14:33:51.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114002437367312423"], "id": "2114002437367312423", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 52, "impression_count": 26164, "like_count": 162, "quote_count": 7, "reply_count": 19, "retweet_count": 37}, "text": "Jason Furman on AI vs human economists: If he were running the CEA today and had a choice between 20 highly qualified staff members “versus the AI systems that we have today, I would somewhat regretfully and sadly choose the AI systems.” https://t.co/nfqsDAngQP", "url": "https://x.com/lisaabramowicz1/status/2114002437367312423"}, {"author_id": "733647469305864195", "created_at": "2026-10-24T09:34:36.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113927127036985651"], "id": "2113927127036985651", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 39, "impression_count": 18914, "like_count": 164, "quote_count": 7, "reply_count": 14, "retweet_count": 27}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2113582190592180729", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "Amazing how many folks still haven't figured out that the tariffs have led Chinese goods (China increasingly exports high value components) to take a one stop flight rather than a non stop flight to the US -- the bilateral data doesn't tell us much\n\n1/2 https://t.co/HrTrKiirMj", "url": "https://x.com/Brad_Setser/status/2113927127036985651"}, {"author_id": "497231011", "created_at": "2026-10-24T04:44:48.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113854194272669707"], "id": "2113854194272669707", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 2, "impression_count": 1790, "like_count": 8, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 2}, "text": "\"Major Chinese AI developers DeepSeek &amp; MiniMax have won state approval for global use of their #AI ‌models, according to CCTV\" https://t.co/TY05dStruB", "url": "https://x.com/ChinaBeigeBook/status/2113854194272669707"}, {"author_id": "14096763", "created_at": "2026-10-24T03:10:17.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113830411830735332"], "id": "2113830411830735332", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 51, "impression_count": 56332, "like_count": 1045, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 33, "retweet_count": 10}, "text": "The Sopranos ep. where Christopher takes an acting class is fascinating. It’s the only time where the viewer stops and thinks “Wow, Imperioli is an incredible actor.” But the thought only pops into your head right then, because you forget he’s acting during the rest of the show.", "url": "https://x.com/TheStalwart/status/2113830411830735332"}, {"author_id": "3512101", "created_at": "2026-10-23T23:59:45.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113782458927714319"], "id": "2113782458927714319", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 5524, "like_count": 3, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 1}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2113772077425541457", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "NCRC https://t.co/P77tgIjU1z", "url": "https://x.com/niubi/status/2113782458927714319"}, {"author_id": "14096763", "created_at": "2026-10-23T23:58:03.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113782032018923712"], "id": "2113782032018923712", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 11, "impression_count": 16901, "like_count": 56, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 9, "retweet_count": 2}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2113780213528092804", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "Tbh idk. But if Dario’s fear is misaligned ASI, then what’s so good about holding back Fable, or coming up with more aggressive bio classifiers? These things seem like a sideshow. https://t.co/nVtJD4Tzh7", "url": "https://x.com/TheStalwart/status/2113782032018923712"}, {"author_id": "14096763", "created_at": "2026-10-23T23:41:47.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113777940072894778"], "id": "2113777940072894778", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 47, "impression_count": 24198, "like_count": 197, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 18, "retweet_count": 11}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2113273917544505798", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "Good post here from Nathan. Sure, Anthropic has taken actions that may have cost it money. But in Dario’s post, there’s a conspicuous absence of any actual pacing or slowing progress towards RSI, despite a widespread view that “alignment” is nowhere close to being solved. https://t.co/sp4Xiuj63x", "url": "https://x.com/TheStalwart/status/2113777940072894778"}, {"author_id": "497231011", "created_at": "2026-10-23T23:14:03.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113770962130981071"], "id": "2113770962130981071", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1799, "like_count": 5, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 2}, "text": "Not stimulus!\nhttps://t.co/jwx2AXd9Q3", "url": "https://x.com/ChinaBeigeBook/status/2113770962130981071"}, {"author_id": "14096763", "created_at": "2026-10-23T22:22:14.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113757919988842545"], "id": "2113757919988842545", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 39, "impression_count": 34232, "like_count": 101, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 6, "retweet_count": 5}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2113735972751843387", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "I’m confident that Don will successfully will “crunch spread” into existence https://t.co/DVDs1bvxFd", "url": "https://x.com/TheStalwart/status/2113757919988842545"}, {"author_id": "14096763", "created_at": "2026-10-23T21:56:01.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113751322331894100"], "id": "2113751322331894100", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 6, "impression_count": 16908, "like_count": 67, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 4, "retweet_count": 2}, "text": "Don't worry, I'll spam this a bunch of times, before then. But... \n\nNEW SHOW ALERT: @LSCCountry, Lucinda's, 10/28\n\nCome out and watch your favorite Lower East Side country band at Manhattan's hottest honky tonk.", "url": "https://x.com/TheStalwart/status/2113751322331894100"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["16_2113750235621285888"]}, "author_id": "702235316812275712", "created_at": "2026-10-23T21:51:43.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113750241367449875"], "id": "2113750241367449875", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2335, "like_count": 12, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 1}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2113668103494328646", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "Current status of the Federal Helium Reserve https://t.co/1Sfl6QV0jn https://t.co/NybWfam2xx", "url": "https://x.com/EconBerger/status/2113750241367449875"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2113749448283099139"]}, "author_id": "3512101", "created_at": "2026-10-23T21:48:36.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113749454033441245"], "id": "2113749454033441245", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 3360, "like_count": 2, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 2, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Good pizza https://t.co/wu32LEidY5", "url": "https://x.com/niubi/status/2113749454033441245"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["13_2113736132865249280"]}, "author_id": "188369814", "created_at": "2026-10-23T20:57:15.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113736533023015217"], "id": "2113736533023015217", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 45, "impression_count": 31298, "like_count": 134, "quote_count": 2, "reply_count": 31, "retweet_count": 13}, "text": "Inflation is Still the Problem\nRational Dissent Episode 014\n\nPost-COVID structural shifts like deglobalization and tariffs have permanently eliminated the cheap goods deflation that previously offset services inflation, leaving the U.S. settled in a 3% inflation world where a 5% https://t.co/f7F6MiTlb0", "url": "https://x.com/biancoresearch/status/2113736533023015217"}, {"author_id": "30034124", "created_at": "2026-10-23T20:32:02.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113730187367964924"], "id": "2113730187367964924", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 2, "impression_count": 2022, "like_count": 47, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 13}, "text": "As Fermilab builds components for its powerful new linear accelerator, engineers are driving innovation by using a collaborative robot to automate the assembly of superconducting cavities, sharply reducing the risk of errors in a cleanroom environment.\nhttps://t.co/sw0sOGL5G2", "url": "https://x.com/Fermilab/status/2113730187367964924"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2113725916207579136"]}, "author_id": "3039504459", "created_at": "2026-10-23T20:15:04.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113725918711566830"], "id": "2113725918711566830", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 14, "impression_count": 2279, "like_count": 33, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 3, "retweet_count": 9}, "text": "#OnTheCover of this week’s issue: Scanning tunneling microscope topographic image of a cluster-decorated Lieb lattice constructed with 57 Fe adatoms on a Ag(111) surface.\n\nCheck out the complete issue: https://t.co/PMcVWkBrvT https://t.co/fqN0AdZyL5", "url": "https://x.com/PhysRevLett/status/2113725918711566830"}], "includes": {"media": [{"media_key": "3_2114058617359843328", "type": "photo"}, {"media_key": "3_2114051631159324672", "type": "photo"}, {"media_key": "3_2114051631121580032", "type": "photo"}, {"media_key": "3_2114023283075031040", "type": "photo"}, {"media_key": "3_2114004270244605952", "type": "photo"}, {"media_key": "16_2113750235621285888", "type": "animated_gif"}, {"media_key": "3_2113749448283099139", "type": "photo"}, {"media_key": "13_2113736132865249280", "type": "video"}, {"media_key": "3_2113725916207579136", "type": "photo"}], "users": [{"id": "497231011", "name": "China Beige Book", "username": "ChinaBeigeBook"}, {"id": "14096763", "name": "Joe Weisenthal", "username": "TheStalwart"}, {"id": "423769635", "name": "(((The Daily Shot)))", "username": "SoberLook"}, {"id": "1327359720", "name": "Lisa Abramowicz", "username": "lisaabramowicz1"}, {"id": "733647469305864195", "name": "Brad Setser", "username": "Brad_Setser"}, {"id": "3512101", "name": "Bill Bishop", "username": "niubi"}, {"id": "702235316812275712", "name": "Guy Berger", "username": "EconBerger"}, {"id": "188369814", "name": "Jim Bianco", "username": "biancoresearch"}, {"id": "30034124", "name": "Fermilab", "username": "Fermilab"}, {"id": "3039504459", "name": "Physical Review Letters", "username": "PhysRevLett"}]}, "meta": {"newest_id": "2114098005934780817", "next_token": "b26v89c19zqg8o3juzlwtxjooamen9k9zvtpi7rcuo7el", "oldest_id": "2113725918711566830", "result_count": 25}}
